---
description: Google Calendar API Integration
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
- Use Google Calendar API v3 for all calendar operations
- Required OAuth 2.0 scopes:
  - calendar.readonly (for personal calendars)
  - calendar.events (for work calendars)
  - calendar.settings.readonly (optional)

- API interaction patterns:
  - Use webhook notifications for real-time updates
  - Implement polling as fallback (every 10-15 minutes)
  - Batch API requests when possible (up to 50 operations)
  - Implement exponential backoff for rate limiting

- Event handling:
  - Personal events → Read only
  - Work calendar → Create/update/delete shadows
  - Shadow events should be marked with specific extended properties
  - Implement conflict detection for manually modified shadows

- Error handling:
  - Retry transient errors with exponential backoff
  - Log persistent errors and notify users
  - Implement circuit breaker pattern for API outages

